{"type":"message","id":"a7e85e21","parentId":"fbe4d478","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:18:51.014Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"216191352","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# MEMORY.md — Knowledge Tracking System Memory\n\n## 🧠 Long-Term Knowledge: The Smart Learning & Analysis Engine\n\n### 🎯 Core Purpose\nA comprehensive knowledge tracking system that:\n1. Tracks daily briefs from @intothecryptoverse YouTube channel\n2. Analyzes videos for key insights and market-moving information\n3. Organizes knowledge into 5 categories with SRS flashcards\n4. Maintains deep summaries for every analyzed video\n\n---\n\n## 📂 Key Files & Their Purpose\n\n### Analysis Engine\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `analyzer.py` | Main analysis logic + **SRS flashcard generation** + categorization engine |\n| `tracker.py` | Video tracking with deep summary generation |\n| `flashcard_history.json` | SRS review scheduling and progress tracking |\n\n### Dashboards\n- **Gaps Dashboard**: Interactive flashcards with category badges, flip-to-reveal answers\n- **Mimic Dashboard**: Premium Cyberpunk HUD for market analysis data\n\n---\n\n## 🏷️ Category System (Implemented 2026-03-14)\n\nEach knowledge piece is tagged with one or more categories:\n\n| Badge | Category | Focus |\n|-------|----------|-------|\n| 📈 | ECONOMICS | Macro trends, inflation data, economic indicators |\n| ₿ | CRYPTO | Bitcoin, altcoins, blockchain developments |\n| 🧮 | MATHEMATICS | Regression analysis, statistical models, quantitative methods |\n| 🏛️ | FED | Interest rates, monetary policy, central banking |\n| 📊 | SP500 | Equities market analysis, S&P performance |\n\n---\n\n## 🔬 Value Flagging System\n\n**🔥 High Value**: Critical information (e.g., major Bitcoin updates, significant economic shifts)\n**⚪ Normal**: Routine updates and standard market commentary\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Spaced Repetition Logic\n\nCards progress through review stages:\n1. **New** → First exposure to a concept\n2. **Learning** → Active study period\n3. **Review Due** → SRS algorithm indicates re-review needed\n4. **Mastered** → Confident recall achieved\n\nReview intervals increase based on performance:\n- Correct answer: Extend interval (e.g., 1 day → 3 days → 7 days → 30 days)\n- Incorrect answer: Reset to earlier stage for reinforcement\n\n---\n\n## 📊 What the System Tracks\n\nFor each video/knowledge piece:\n- ✅ Date analyzed\n- ✅ Primary category (with badges for multi-tagging)\n- 🔥 High Value flag\n- 💡 Benjamin Cowen-style answers stored\n- 📅 Last review date (SRS scheduling)\n- 🔄 Review count and mastery level\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Important Notes\n\n1. **Daily Brief Migration**: The `mimic` repo will be remade with future data when Benjamin stops YouTube content\n2. **GitHub Pages Deployment**: All dashboards deploy via GitHub Pages workflows\n3. **Telegram Integration**: Primary platform for link sharing and briefs\n4. **Riyadh Timezone**: All operations scheduled according to Asia/Riyadh (GMT+3)\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 System Health Check\n\nBefore each major operation, verify:\n- [ ] Gateway service running on port 18789\n- [ ] LM Studio health at `http://100.67.202.80:3003/v1`\n- [ ] All Python scripts have execute permissions\n- [ ] GitHub Pages workflows are active for dashboard repos\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773479931013}}
{"type":"message","id":"f53d383c","parentId":"a7e85e21","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:19:42.156Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Based on my search, this cron job is designed to process daily briefs from the @intothecryptoverse YouTube channel. However:\n\n1. The web_search failed due to missing Brave API key\n2. Memory search returned no results about specific scripts for processing these briefs\n3. The workspace doesn't contain obvious Python analysis scripts (analyzer.py, tracker.py mentioned in MEMORY.md)\n\nThis appears to be a system event that triggers hourly at :25, but I don't have the actual implementation details or the input data to process. The job is currently empty - it's just a scheduled trigger with no defined task payload or operation parameters."},{"type":"text","text":"## Summary: Daily Brief Processing Job Status\n\nThe cron job `[a0036b1a-bb1b-428f-a028-06ab983a1287]` is configured to run **every hour at :25** for processing daily brief content from @intothecryptoverse YouTube channel.\n\n### Current Status: ⚠️ No Payload Defined\n\nThis job appears to be a scheduled trigger without an actual payload or operation specified in the message. To process daily briefs, I would need:\n\n1. **Input Data**: The URL/content of the latest brief from @intothecryptoverse\n2. **Processing Logic**: Either:\n   - A Python script (analyzer.py/tracker.py mentioned in MEMORY.md)\n   - Or instructions on what analysis to perform\n\n### Suggested Next Steps\n\n**Option 1**: If you have a brief URL to analyze, provide it and I can:\n- Fetch the content using web_fetch\n- Apply market analysis logic (economic indicators, crypto signals, etc.)\n- Generate flashcards via SRS algorithm\n- Tag with appropriate categories (📈 ECONOMICS, ₿ CRYPTO, 🏛️ FED, etc.)\n\n**Option 2**: If this should integrate with existing scripts, please share:\n- The GitHub repos (mimic/gaps) for context\n- Any processing instructions or output format required\n\n---\n\n*Waiting for payload/input to execute the brief analysis operation.*"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen3-5-9b","model":"qwen3.5-9b-claude-4.6-opus-reasoning-distilled","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773479931014}}
